diff --git a/HISTORY.md b/HISTORY.md
index bcc8f04..d95bd4f 100644
--- a/HISTORY.md
+++ b/HISTORY.md
@@ -26,6 +26,17 @@ Our backwards-compatibility policy can be found [here](https://github.com/python
   ([#732](https://github.com/python-attrs/cattrs/pull/732))
 - Support running the test suite without `cbor2` installed.
   ([#748](https://github.com/python-attrs/cattrs/pull/748))
+- Fix generated hooks breaking (or silently corrupting keys) when renamed keys or _TypedDict_ keys contain quotes, backslashes or newlines.
+- `Converter.copy()` now keeps structure hooks registered for unions and the fallback hook factories.
+  Mapping hooks of copied preconf converters and union passthrough hooks now use the copy instead of the original converter.
+- Fix namedtuples with stringified annotations and namedtuple subclasses.
+- Fix enums with stringified `_value_` annotations, and dataclasses with stringified `Annotated[T, override()]` annotations.
+- {func}`cattrs.subclasses.subclasses` no longer drops non-slotted subclasses of slotted dataclasses, and filters out pre-slotting _attrs_ classes.
+- `Literal[1]` no longer accepts `True` (and vice versa), including in {func}`cattrs.strategies.configure_union_passthrough`.
+- Fix `TypedDict` overrides inside `Required` and outside `NotRequired`, and `Counter` keys not being unstructured using the key type.
+- The `BaseConverter` now handles `init=False` and `kw_only` _attrs_ fields when structuring.
+- Fix formatting {class}`cattrs.ForbiddenExtraKeysError` and {func}`cattrs.transform_error` with non-string keys and argument-less exceptions.
+- Using the hook registration decorators without the required annotations now raises a `TypeError` instead of registering a useless hook.
 
 ## 26.1.0 (2026-02-18)
 
